WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.320
Clear ownership prevents findings from stalling between teams.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.700
Application owners usually manage code, dependencies, and deployment behavior.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.320
Platform teams manage nodes, runtimes, and Kubernetes components.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.340
Security maintains policy, intelligence, prioritization guidance, and oversight.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:21.160
Registries and build systems also need named owners.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.060
Patch service-level agreements should reflect risk, exposure,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.600
and criticality rather than severity alone.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.460
Define when the clock starts, what counts as remediation, who verifies closure,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.040
and how newly exploited conditions change the target date.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:41.380
Exceptions and risk acceptance are documented decisions, not silent delay.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:47.760
Record affected assets, residual risk, rationale, compensating controls, approver, owner,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.460
expiration, and review trigger.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.920
An exception should return to the remediation queue when its conditions change.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.820
Reporting should connect vulnerabilities to deployed environments and owners.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.320
Useful views include aging critical findings, overdue items, stale images,

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.340
unpatched base-image descendants, unsupported components, exception age,

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.720
and the difference between fixed images and workloads still running old digests.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:19.540
Metrics should measure effectiveness: time from disclosure to triage, rebuild, deployment,

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.440
and verified closure; percentage remediated within target;

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.500
recurrence caused by stale templates; production coverage;

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.040
and failed or rolled-back updates.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.540
Raw finding counts can rise when visibility improves.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.720
Governance turns security debt into visible choices.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.260
Review trends with engineering and leadership,

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.720
fund recurring base-image and platform maintenance, remove abandoned artifacts,

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.580
and improve the process where delays repeat.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.320
The aim is reliable risk reduction, not perfect dashboards.
